.TH "EPX\-SHOPPING\-LISTS" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-shopping\-lists \- read, create, replace and delete customers\(aq shopping lists
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shopping\-lists [flags]
epx shopping\-lists [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads customers\(aq shopping lists, personal data included: each customer\(aqs lists by name, with how many items they hold. Items are only in \fB\-o json\fR. CUSTOMER is the customer id the lists are kept under (the reference calls it the customer number; for a customer that Emporix numbered, the two are the same); get takes it, and a customer without shopping lists is not found. create, update and delete create, replace and delete a customer\(aqs lists.
.PP
Its reads require the shoppinglist.shoppinglist_read scope. Its writes require the shoppinglist.shoppinglist_manage scope.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx shopping\-lists create"
Create a shopping list of a customer.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shopping\-lists create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates the shopping list in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON object with the customerId of the customer it belongs to, the list\(aqs name and its items (each with its id, productId and quantity), and prints what Emporix answers with: the customer\(aqs id. A list of that name that the customer has already is a conflict (exit 5). Emporix does not check the customer: it creates the list of an unknown customer id too.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the shoppinglist.shoppinglist_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shopping\-lists create \-\-file list.json \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.SS "epx shopping\-lists delete"
Delete a shopping list of a customer.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shopping\-lists delete CUSTOMER [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the shopping list \fB\-\-name\fR of CUSTOMER; its other lists stay. A customer without shopping lists, or without a list of that name, is not found (exit 4). \fBepx shopping\-lists get CUSTOMER\fR shows the lists that are left.
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type CUSTOMER at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the shoppinglist.shoppinglist_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-name <NAME>\fR
The NAME of the list to delete (required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx shopping\-lists delete\-all"
Delete every shopping list of a customer.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shopping\-lists delete\-all CUSTOMER [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes every shopping list of CUSTOMER. A customer without shopping lists is not found (exit 4).
.PP
Deletes every shopping list of the customer with one request, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type CUSTOMER at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the shoppinglist.shoppinglist_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx shopping\-lists get"
Show one customer\(aqs shopping lists.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shopping\-lists get CUSTOMER [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads customers\(aq shopping lists, personal data included: each customer\(aqs lists by name, with how many items they hold. Items are only in \fB\-o json\fR. CUSTOMER is the customer id the lists are kept under (the reference calls it the customer number; for a customer that Emporix numbered, the two are the same); get takes it, and a customer without shopping lists is not found.
.PP
Requires the shoppinglist.shoppinglist_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among CUSTOMER, LISTS.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx shopping\-lists list"
List customers\(aq shopping lists.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shopping\-lists list [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads customers\(aq shopping lists, personal data included: each customer\(aqs lists by name, with how many items they hold. Items are only in \fB\-o json\fR. CUSTOMER is the customer id the lists are kept under (the reference calls it the customer number; for a customer that Emporix numbered, the two are the same); get takes it, and a customer without shopping lists is not found.
.PP
Requires the shoppinglist.shoppinglist_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among CUSTOMER, LISTS.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx shopping\-lists update"
Replace a shopping list of a customer.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx shopping\-lists update CUSTOMER [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the shopping list of CUSTOMER that the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR names with it: an object with the list\(aqs name and its items (each with its id, productId and quantity). Send its metadata.version as read to replace it only if nobody changed it since: Emporix answers 409 Conflict (exit 5) otherwise. A customer without shopping lists, or without a list of that name, is not found (exit 4). Update creates no list; create does.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the shoppinglist.shoppinglist_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
